    "repo": "rails/rails",
    "commit": "dbafc460fa",
    "message": "Remove Ruby < 3.3 compatibility code

This commit removes Ruby < 3.3 compatibility code since Rails main
branch requires Ruby 3.3.

- No need to check `SecureRandom.method(:alphanumeric).parameters.size`
  in Ruby 3.3+ because it is always 2
https://github.com/ruby/securerandom/pull/36

- Ruby 3.3 introduces `Range#overlap?`
https://bugs.ruby-lang.org/issues/19839

- Ruby 3.3 introcuces `Fiber#kill`
https://bugs.ruby-lang.org/issues/595

Refer to https://github.com/rails/rails/pull/56511"
  },
  "model": "jev-latest",
  "questions": {
    "claim": {
      "type": "noul",
      "instructions": "The author of this commit wrote: "- No need to check `SecureRandom.method(:alphanumeric).parameters.size` in Ruby 3.3+ because it is always 2 https://github.com/ruby/securerandom/pull/36". Taking "always" literally, does the claim hold as written?"
    }
  }
}
